  <p>
    The app itself can hold up to 10 stored eSIM profiles on one device, which matters if you keep old destination eSIMs around instead of deleting them after every trip.
  </p>

  <!-- Local-network plans: figures verified on SimLocal's own plan pages, October 2026 -->
  <h2>SimLocal in Vietnam and Japan: Plans on a Named Local Network</h2>
  <p>
    In two destinations SimLocal sells plans that run on one specific local carrier instead of a generic roaming partner. The prices below are what SimLocal's own plan pages showed in October 2026. We haven't bought either plan ourselves, and the partnership claims are SimLocal's own words, not something we've independently confirmed.
  </p>

  <h3>Vietnam: MobiFone</h3>
  <p>
    SimLocal says it is an official MobiFone partner and that these plans run on MobiFone's own network. It also told its affiliates in mid-October 2026 that it had lowered its Vietnam prices.
  </p>
  <div class="content-box">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Validity</th><th>High-speed data</th><th>Price</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>75 GB</td><td>15 days</td><td>5 GB per day</td><td>US$19</td></tr>
        <tr><td>180 GB</td><td>30 days</td><td>6 GB per day</td><td>US$29</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="content-note">The 75 GB page lists data, calls and SMS; the 180 GB page lists data and calls. Hotspot is supported on compatible devices. SimLocal says MobiFone covers all major cities and areas like Sapa, Ha Giang and the Mekong Delta, but admits signal can be weaker in remote mountain areas. Its pages don't say what happens after the daily high-speed allowance runs out.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Japan: au by KDDI</h3>
  <p>
    SimLocal's Japan page says it is the only provider in Europe offering official au Japan eSIM plans online, and its FAQ says au covers 99% of the populated area. There are four plans, all labelled "Unlimited eSIM" and 4G/5G:
  </p>
  <div class="content-box">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Validity</th><th>Price</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>4 days</td><td>US$13</td></tr>
        <tr><td>7 days</td><td>US$19</td></tr>
        <tr><td>10 days</td><td>US$26</td></tr>
        <tr><td>15 days</td><td>US$39</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="content-note">The plan pages don't state a data volume, whether hotspot works, or whether calls and SMS are included. SimLocal's page also claims 10 GB of high-speed data a day against rivals that throttle after 1 to 3 GB, but doesn't say whether that applies to these au plans. Ask SimLocal support before you rely on it for a heavy-data trip.</p>
  </div>
  <p>
    We've only tested our own code on a UK plan, so check that the discount shows at checkout before you pay for a Vietnam or Japan plan.
  </p>

